// The opposite-sign twin of 00, and the reason the fix has to be on
// both sides: the kernel's over-limit CLAMP also clobbers its length
// memory, so the divergence outlives the over-limit cycle.
//
// `emit_init_loop` (fusion/emit/scaffold.rs ~912) does
// `let n = select(oversize, zero, n)` and then feeds that CLAMPED n to
// `flags.set_len(n)` (~913) and `open_slot_tables(sel_sites, n, ...)`
// (~918) — so the per-instance prev-length word records 0 for the
// over-limit cycle. The interp, which never entered its resize branch at
// all (00), still remembers length 1.
//
// Epoch 1: count=1 -> both emit [0].
// Epoch 2: count=16777217 (one over the limit) -> both quiet.
// Epoch 3: count=1 again.
//   interp: retained length is still 1, the source length is 1, so
//           nothing resized and the const callback body is quiet -> NO
//           emission (correct under the kernel's own documented firing
//           rule: fire iff resized OR a slot fired OR the source fired
//           empty).
//   jit:    prev-length word says 0, so 0 -> 1 reads as a RESIZE and it
//           fires [0] — a phantom fire caused purely by the clamp
//           having overwritten the length memory two cycles earlier.
//
// Fix: see 00 — the kernel must leave length/prev-length/slot state
// untouched on an over-limit count (taint the result only), and the
// interp must force taint so the over-limit cycle is bottom on both
// sides.
// schedule-v1: cap=32 events=256; in0=i64:1; in0=i64:16777217; in0=i64:1
array::init(in0, |i| i64:0)
